  -m "ADR-153 asked whether anything READS what a page hands over; ADR-208 asked whether a button that is supposed to hand something over hands anything over at all. Both are questions about the CHANNEL and neither one opens the envelope. OF THE 317 FIGURES THE EXPORTING PAGES OF THIS KIT COMPUTE AND PUT ON THE SCREEN, 132 APPEARED IN NOTHING THOSE PAGES HAND OVER. The ethogram had three exports of a scored session and Cohen's kappa, the raw agreement and the agreement expected by chance were in none of them. The soil bench exported its mix recipe and not one of the fourteen figures of its compost log: a pile logged for a month left no file at all. The selection log's study sheet carried n, mean, SD and R per trait -- the INPUTS to the analysis and not the analysis. Every audit in this kit was green while this was true, by construction, because nobody had ever put the two readings side by side. tools/audit_carried.py replays each page's own task, presses every control that hands something over (audit_outputs' rule, asked rather than copied), collects the payloads and checks every figure read-report sees against them. Most of the file is about what counts as the same number: 6.00x10^5 on screen is 600000 in a CSV, the comparison is made at the SCREEN's precision and WITHIN its last digit rather than by rounding both sides to it (double rounding, ADR-087's shape, arriving in the instrument), and the exponent counts. The bias is towards CARRIED on purpose, so every LOST is a figure whose value appears nowhere in anything the page hands over. Twelve pages now hand their own analysis over; the soil bench needed an export it did not have and its task was extended to press it and hold the bytes. Three figures are declared right to stay on the screen with their reasons. verify_carried 44, mutate_carried 24 with one recorded equivalent. 132 to 32, and the 32 are one page: the ecology lab's export is a .eco PROTOCOL and by design carries inputs and hypotheses rather than results." `
